### Create employee / Test 1 - Duplicate email
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Masud",
  "lastName": "Ikbal",
  "email": "masud.cseu@gmail.com",
  "phone": "+8801712243940"
}

###Test 2 — Invalid email
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Masud",
  "lastName": "Ikbal",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "phone": "+8801712345678"
}

###Test 3 — Missing first name
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Ikbal",
  "email": "another@example.com",
  "phone": "+8801712345678"
}

###Test A — Retrieve one customer
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers/f8e4ae8f-596a-4d0d-9c51-ce9714530886

###Test B — Customer does not exist
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

###Test C — Retrieve all customers
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers?page=0&size=10

###Test D — Invalid pagination
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers?page=-1&size=10

###Test A — Update customer
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers/f8e4ae8f-596a-4d0d-9c51-ce9714530886
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Masud",
  "lastName": "Ikbal",
  "email": "masud.updated@example.com",
  "phone": "+8801812345678",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

###Test B — Deactivate customer
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers/f8e4ae8f-596a-4d0d-9c51-ce9714530886/deactivate


